End-to-end connectivity between PC0 (20.1.1.10) and PC12 (120.1.1.10) is currently healthy. Live tests show 0% loss both ways, with sub‑millisecond RTTs. The control-plane routes are present and consistent: on r1, 120.0.0.0/8 is learned via OSPF from r11 over B (r1.eth1 111.1.1.x). r11 is redistributing EIGRP and connected into OSPF, and r12 advertises 120.0.0.0/8 via EIGRP over EE (r12.eth0 112.1.1.2 to r11.eth0 112.1.1.1). PC12 has a default via 120.1.1.1.

